body:
This bug comes with a Perl interpreter (curl bindings), I haven't managed to find another way to reproduce the bug 😞 That said, the same assertion failure has been seen by someone not using the bindings, and the behavior definitely changed in the last few releases, so I'm fairly convinced the issue isn't with the bindings (or at least it would be doing something wrong that was not wrong before).

Steps to reproduce:

    # build curl statically
    ./configure --with-nghttp2=/home/tom/code/nghttp2-lib --enable-debug --disable-shared --enable-static --with-pic --prefix=/home/tom/code/curl-lib --with-zlib
    make -j8 install

    # clone and run the Perl code
    git clone --branch curlbug-report https://github.com/TvdW/perl-AnyEvent-YACurl
    cd perl-AnyEvent-YACurl/AnyEvent-YACurl/
    CURL_CONFIG=/home/tom/code/curl-lib/bin/curl-config perl Makefile.PL
    make
    perl -Mblib t/curlbug.t  >/dev/null

I wish I had an easier way to reproduce this, but... 😢

